<title>USA: QMS says cutting workforce by 15 percent.</title>
<headline>QMS says cutting workforce by 15 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MOBILE, Ala 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>QMS Inc said on Thursday that it was reducing its nationwide workforce by roughly 100 employees, or 15 percent.</p>
<p>Of the 100 employees, 55 will be cut from the company's Mobile headquarters, the print systems maker said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;This action is being taken in order to align expenses more closely with current revenues and to accommodate changes in the nature of the company's business operations requirements,&quot; QMS said of the cuts, adding that they were designed &quot;to return the company to profitability early in fiscal year 1998.&quot;</p>
</text>
